IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `uc-core`
IMPORT `uc-core-persons`
IMPORT `uc1-common`

-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Part 1, introduction: the dates in the title block and regulation 1,
-- and regulations 3 to 6 (couples, responsibility for a child or qualifying young person, qualifying young persons, rounding).
-- Regulation 2 and the rounding rules of regulation 6(1) and (1A) are the keel's (uc-core*.l4).
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt, a plain-text rendering of the revised text (legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-07-16)
-- made by a converter script. It is not the official text. Every `-- src:N | ...` line copies line N of that file.
-- Target: the stable build 1.6.98. Seat: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, alone or as one of a couple.
--
-- Facts that other provisions decide stay plain inputs here, each commented where it matters: whether a person is a member of a
-- couple at all is section 39 of the Act (not among the inputs); the basic conditions are section 4 of the Act. The regulation 2
-- definitions are the keel's. A rule here takes a defined term as a plain yes or no, and the seat builds the keel's record from plain
-- facts and passes in the result of the keel's rule for "terminally ill", "prisoner", "looked after by a local authority" and
-- "foster parent" (see "Seat" in NOTES.md for the places where it does not).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 1 and the title block: the dates.

-- src:4 | Made 25th February 2013
@ref Made 25th February 2013 (src:4)
`reg 1 — the day on which these Regulations were made` MEANS YMD 2013 2 25

-- src:5 | Coming into force 29th April 2013
-- src:11 | These Regulations may be cited as the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 and come into force on 29th April 2013.
@ref reg 1 (src:5-11)
`reg 1 — the day on which these Regulations come into force` MEANS YMD 2013 4 29

-- src:5 | Coming into force 29th April 2013
-- src:11 | These Regulations may be cited as the Universal Credit Regulations 2013 and come into force on 29th April 2013.
@ref reg 1 (src:5-11)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 1 — these Regulations are in force on a day` day MEANS
    day AT LEAST `reg 1 — the day on which these Regulations come into force`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 3: couples.

-- (2) A couple may be entitled as joint claimants where (a) one member does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(b) (under
-- the qualifying age for state pension credit) if the other does; or (b) one member does not meet the basic condition in section
-- 4(1)(d) (not receiving education) and is not excepted from it, if the other meets it or is excepted from it.
-- src:120 | (2) A couple may be entitled to universal credit as joint claimants where—
-- src:121 | (a) one member does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(b) (under the qualifying age for state pension credit) if the other member does meet that condition; or
-- src:122 | (b) one member does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(d) (not receiving education) and is not excepted from that condition if the other member does meet that condition or is excepted from it.
@ref reg 3(2) (src:120-122)
DECLARE `Member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(b) and (d)` HAS
    `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(b), under the qualifying age for state pension credit`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Act, sections 4, 5 or 22 (not a piece)
    `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(d), not receiving education`                          IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Act, sections 4, 5 or 22 (not a piece)
    `is excepted from the basic condition in section 4(1)(d) by regulation 14`                       IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:121 | (a) one member does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(b) (under the qualifying age for state pension credit) if the other member does meet that condition; or
@ref reg 3(2)(a) (src:121)
GIVEN `the member who does not meet the condition` IS A `Member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(b) and (d)`
      `the other member` IS A `Member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(b) and (d)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(2)(a) — one member does not meet the age condition and the other does` `the member who does not meet the condition` `the other member` MEANS
    (NOT (`the member who does not meet the condition`'s `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(b), under the qualifying age for state pension credit`))
    AND (`the other member`'s `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(b), under the qualifying age for state pension credit`)

-- src:122 | (b) one member does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(d) (not receiving education) and is not excepted from that condition if the other member does meet that condition or is excepted from it.
@ref reg 3(2)(b) (src:122)
GIVEN `the member who does not meet the condition` IS A `Member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(b) and (d)`
      `the other member` IS A `Member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(b) and (d)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(2)(b) — one member is receiving education and is not excepted, and the other is not or is excepted` `the member who does not meet the condition` `the other member` MEANS
    ((NOT (`the member who does not meet the condition`'s `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(d), not receiving education`))
     AND (NOT (`the member who does not meet the condition`'s `is excepted from the basic condition in section 4(1)(d) by regulation 14`)))
    AND ((`the other member`'s `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(d), not receiving education`)
         OR (`the other member`'s `is excepted from the basic condition in section 4(1)(d) by regulation 14`))

-- src:120 | (2) A couple may be entitled to universal credit as joint claimants where—
-- src:121 | (a) one member does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(b) (under the qualifying age for state pension credit) if the other member does meet that condition; or
-- src:122 | (b) one member does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(d) (not receiving education) and is not excepted from that condition if the other member does meet that condition or is excepted from it.
@ref reg 3(2) (src:120-122)
GIVEN first IS A `Member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(b) and (d)`
      second IS A `Member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(b) and (d)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(2) — a couple may be entitled as joint claimants despite a basic condition` first second MEANS
    (`reg 3(2)(a) — one member does not meet the age condition and the other does` first second)
    OR (`reg 3(2)(a) — one member does not meet the age condition and the other does` second first)
    OR (`reg 3(2)(b) — one member is receiving education and is not excepted, and the other is not or is excepted` first second)
    OR (`reg 3(2)(b) — one member is receiving education and is not excepted, and the other is not or is excepted` second first)

-- (3) A member of a couple may make a claim as a single person if the other member (a) does not meet the basic condition in section
-- 4(1)(a) (at least 18) and is not a person in respect of whom the minimum age in regulation 8 applies; (b) does not meet the basic
-- condition in section 4(1)(c) (in Great Britain); (c) is a prisoner; (d) is a person other than a prisoner in respect of whom
-- entitlement does not arise by virtue of regulation 19; or (e) is a person to whom section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act
-- 1999 applies.
-- src:123 | (3) A person who is a member of a couple may make a claim as a single person if the other member of the couple—
-- src:124 | (a) does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(a) (at least 18 years old) and is not a person in respect of whom the minimum age specified in regulation 8 applies;
-- src:125 | (b) does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(c) (in Great Britain);
-- src:126 | (c) is a prisoner;. . .
-- src:127 | (d) is a person other than a prisoner in respect of whom entitlement does not arise by virtue of regulation 19 (restrictions on entitlement) ; or
-- src:128 | (e) is a person to whom section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 (exclusion from benefits) applies,
@ref reg 3(3) (src:123-128)
DECLARE `Other member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(a) and (c)` HAS
    `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(a), at least 18 years old`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Act, sections 4, 5 or 22 (not a piece)
    `is a person in respect of whom the minimum age specified in regulation 8 applies`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(c), in Great Britain`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: the Act, sections 4, 5 or 22 (not a piece)
    `is a prisoner`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a person in respect of whom entitlement does not arise by virtue of regulation 19`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a person to whom section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 applies`    IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: immigration law and the EEA Regulations (not a piece)

-- src:123 | (3) A person who is a member of a couple may make a claim as a single person if the other member of the couple—
-- src:124 | (a) does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(a) (at least 18 years old) and is not a person in respect of whom the minimum age specified in regulation 8 applies;
-- src:125 | (b) does not meet the basic condition in section 4(1)(c) (in Great Britain);
-- src:126 | (c) is a prisoner;. . .
-- src:127 | (d) is a person other than a prisoner in respect of whom entitlement does not arise by virtue of regulation 19 (restrictions on entitlement) ; or
-- src:128 | (e) is a person to whom section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 (exclusion from benefits) applies,
-- src:129 | and regulations 18 (capital limit), 36 (amount of elements) and 22 (deduction of income and work allowance) provide for the calculation of the award in such cases.
@ref reg 3(3) (src:123-129)
GIVEN other IS AN `Other member of a couple and the basic conditions of section 4(1)(a) and (c)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(3) — a member of a couple may make a claim as a single person` other MEANS
    `limb (a)` OR `limb (b)` OR `limb (c)` OR `limb (d)` OR `limb (e)`
    WHERE
        `limb (a)` MEANS
            (NOT (other's `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(a), at least 18 years old`))
            AND (NOT (other's `is a person in respect of whom the minimum age specified in regulation 8 applies`))
        `limb (b)` MEANS NOT (other's `meets the basic condition in section 4(1)(c), in Great Britain`)
        `limb (c)` MEANS other's `is a prisoner`
        `limb (d)` MEANS
            (NOT (other's `is a prisoner`))
            AND (other's `is a person in respect of whom entitlement does not arise by virtue of regulation 19`)
        `limb (e)` MEANS other's `is a person to whom section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 applies`

-- (5) A polygamous marriage is a marriage during which a party to it is married to more than one person and which took place
-- under the laws of a country which permits polygamy.
-- src:134 | (5) In paragraph (4) “polygamous marriage” means a marriage during which a party to it is married to more than one person and which took place under the laws of a country which permits polygamy.
@ref reg 3(5) (src:134)
GIVEN `a party to the marriage is married to more than one person during it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the marriage took place under the laws of a country which permits polygamy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(5) — a polygamous marriage` `a party to the marriage is married to more than one person during it` `the marriage took place under the laws of a country which permits polygamy` MEANS
    (`a party to the marriage is married to more than one person during it`)
    AND (`the marriage took place under the laws of a country which permits polygamy`)

-- (4) Where two people are parties to a polygamous marriage, the fact that they are husband and wife is disregarded if (a) one of them
-- is a party to an earlier marriage that still subsists and (b) the other party to that earlier marriage is living in the same
-- household; the person who is not a party to the earlier marriage may then claim as a single person.
-- src:130 | (4) Where two people are parties to a polygamous marriage, the fact that they are husband and wife is to be disregarded if—
-- src:131 | (a) one of them is a party to an earlier marriage that still subsists; and
-- src:132 | (b) the other party to that earlier marriage is living in the same household,
-- src:133 | and, accordingly, the person who is not a party to the earlier marriage may make a claim for universal credit as a single person.
@ref reg 3(4) (src:130-133)
GIVEN `the two people are parties to a polygamous marriage` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of them is a party to an earlier marriage that still subsists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other party to that earlier marriage is living in the same household` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(4) — the fact that they are husband and wife is disregarded` `the two people are parties to a polygamous marriage` `one of them is a party to an earlier marriage that still subsists` `the other party to that earlier marriage is living in the same household` MEANS
    (`the two people are parties to a polygamous marriage`)
    AND (`one of them is a party to an earlier marriage that still subsists`)
    AND (`the other party to that earlier marriage is living in the same household`)

-- (6) Where the claimant is a member of a couple and the other member is temporarily absent from the claimant's household, they
-- cease to be treated as a couple if the absence is expected to exceed, or does exceed, 6 months.
-- src:135 | (6) Where the claimant is a member of a couple, and the other member is temporarily absent from the claimant's household, they cease to be treated as a couple if that absence is expected to exceed, or does exceed, 6 months.
@ref reg 3(6) (src:135)
GIVEN absence IS AN `Absence that is measured against a limit`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 3(6) — the members of a couple cease to be treated as a couple` absence MEANS
    `uc1 — the absence is expected to exceed or does exceed a time limit` absence (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months)

-- The basis on which a person claims (fork F-3-BASIS, assumed and not ruled): the text says a member of a couple "may" claim as a
-- single person in the paragraph (3) cases and that a couple "may" be entitled jointly in the paragraph (2) cases. The rule reads
-- paragraph (3) first (a member of a couple whose partner is in one of its cases claims as a single person), then a joint claim
-- where each member meets the basic conditions or paragraph (2) applies, and otherwise returns no claim basis (NOTHING).
-- src:119 | (1) This regulation makes provision in relation to couples, including cases where both members of a couple may be entitled to universal credit jointly without each of them meeting all the basic conditions referred to in section 4 of the Act (see paragraph (2)) and cases where a person whose partner does not meet all the basic conditions or is otherwise excluded from entitlement to universal credit may make a claim as a single person (see paragraph (3)).
-- src:123 | (3) A person who is a member of a couple may make a claim as a single person if the other member of the couple—
-- src:128 | (e) is a person to whom section 115 of the Immigration and Asylum Act 1999 (exclusion from benefits) applies,
@ref reg 3(1), (2) and (3) (src:119-128)
GIVEN `the person is a member of a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (3) lets the person claim as a single person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each member meets all the basic conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) applies to the couple` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Claim basis`
`reg 3 — the basis on which the person claims` `the person is a member of a couple` `paragraph (3) lets the person claim as a single person` `each member meets all the basic conditions` `paragraph (2) applies to the couple` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person is a member of a couple`) THEN JUST `a single claimant`
        IF `paragraph (3) lets the person claim as a single person` THEN JUST `a single claimant who is a member of a couple`
        IF (`each member meets all the basic conditions`) OR (`paragraph (2) applies to the couple`) THEN JUST `joint claimants`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 4: when a person is responsible for a child or qualifying young person.

-- (6) Subject to regulation 4A, a child or qualifying young person is treated as not being the responsibility of any person during
-- any period when looked after by a local authority (except a period regulation 4A excludes) or a prisoner.
-- src:144 | (6) Subject to regulation 4A, a child or qualifying young person is to be treated as not being the responsibility of any person during any period when the child or qualifying young person is—
-- src:145 | (a) looked after by a local authority; or
-- src:146 | (b) a prisoner,
@ref reg 4(6) (src:144-146)
GIVEN `the child or qualifying young person is looked after by a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period is excluded from regulation 4(6)(a) by regulation 4A` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child or qualifying young person is a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(6) — the child or qualifying young person is treated as not being the responsibility of any person` `the child or qualifying young person is looked after by a local authority` `the period is excluded from regulation 4(6)(a) by regulation 4A` `the child or qualifying young person is a prisoner` MEANS
    `looked after by a local authority in a period that regulation 4A does not exclude`
    OR (`the child or qualifying young person is a prisoner`)
    WHERE
        `looked after by a local authority in a period that regulation 4A does not exclude` MEANS
            (`the child or qualifying young person is looked after by a local authority`)
            AND (NOT `the period is excluded from regulation 4(6)(a) by regulation 4A`)

-- (7) Where a child or qualifying young person is temporarily absent from a person's household, the person ceases to be responsible
-- if (a) the absence is expected to exceed, or does exceed, 6 months, or (b) the absence is from Great Britain and is expected to
-- exceed, or does exceed, one month, unless it is in circumstances where an absence of a person for longer than one month would be
-- disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2) or (3).
-- src:148 | (7) Where a child or qualifying young person is temporarily absent from a person's household the person ceases to be responsible for the child or qualifying young person if—
-- src:149 | (a) the absence is expected to exceed, or does exceed, 6 months; or
-- src:150 | (b) the absence is from Great Britain and is expected to exceed, or does exceed, one month unless it is in circumstances where an absence of a person for longer than one month would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2) or (3) (medical treatment or convalescence or death of close relative etc.).
@ref reg 4(7) (src:148-150)
GIVEN absence IS AN `Absence that is measured against a limit`
      `the absence is from Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an absence of a person for longer than one month would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(7) — the person ceases to be responsible because of a temporary absence` absence `the absence is from Great Britain` `an absence of a person for longer than one month would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2) or (3)` MEANS
    (`uc1 — the absence is expected to exceed or does exceed a time limit` absence (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 6, unit IS months))
    OR ((`the absence is from Great Britain`)
        AND (`uc1 — the absence is expected to exceed or does exceed a time limit` absence (`Time limit` WITH quantity IS 1, unit IS months))
        AND (NOT `an absence of a person for longer than one month would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2) or (3)`))

-- (2) to (5) and the whole: a person is responsible for a child or qualifying young person who normally lives with them (2), but not
-- for a qualifying young person if the two are living as a couple (3); where the child or young person normally lives with two or
-- more persons who are not a couple, only the one with the main responsibility, by their joint nomination or the Secretary of
-- State's determination (4) and (5); and not at all in the (6) and (7) cases.
-- src:138 | (2) A person is responsible for a child or qualifying young person who normally lives with them.
-- src:139 | (3) But a person is not responsible for a qualifying young person if the two of them are living as a couple.
-- src:140 | (4) Where a child or qualifying young person normally lives with two or more persons who are not a couple, only one of them is to be treated as responsible and that is the person who has the main responsibility.
-- src:141 | (5) The persons mentioned in paragraph (4) may jointly nominate which of them has the main responsibility but the Secretary of State may determine that question—
-- src:142 | (a) in default of agreement; or
-- src:143 | (b) if a nomination or change of nomination does not, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, reflect the arrangements between those persons.
@ref reg 4(2) to (5) (src:138-143)
DECLARE `Child or qualifying young person and the person who may be responsible` HAS
    `the child or qualifying young person normally lives with the person`                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child or qualifying young person is a qualifying young person`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person and the qualifying young person are living as a couple`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the child or qualifying young person normally lives with two or more persons who are not a couple`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has the main responsibility, by nomination under paragraph (5) or by the Secretary of State's determination`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:138 | (2) A person is responsible for a child or qualifying young person who normally lives with them.
-- src:139 | (3) But a person is not responsible for a qualifying young person if the two of them are living as a couple.
-- src:140 | (4) Where a child or qualifying young person normally lives with two or more persons who are not a couple, only one of them is to be treated as responsible and that is the person who has the main responsibility.
-- src:141 | (5) The persons mentioned in paragraph (4) may jointly nominate which of them has the main responsibility but the Secretary of State may determine that question—
-- src:142 | (a) in default of agreement; or
-- src:143 | (b) if a nomination or change of nomination does not, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, reflect the arrangements between those persons.
@ref reg 4(2) to (5) (src:138-143)
GIVEN household IS A `Child or qualifying young person and the person who may be responsible`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4(2) to (5) — the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person apart from paragraphs (6) and (7)` household MEANS
    (household's `the child or qualifying young person normally lives with the person`)
    AND (NOT ((household's `the child or qualifying young person is a qualifying young person`)
              AND (household's `the person and the qualifying young person are living as a couple`)))
    AND ((NOT (household's `the child or qualifying young person normally lives with two or more persons who are not a couple`))
         OR (household's `the person has the main responsibility, by nomination under paragraph (5) or by the Secretary of State's determination`))

-- src:137 | (1) Whether a person is responsible for a child or qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 1 of the Act and these Regulations is determined as follows.
-- src:138 | (2) A person is responsible for a child or qualifying young person who normally lives with them.
-- src:139 | (3) But a person is not responsible for a qualifying young person if the two of them are living as a couple.
-- src:140 | (4) Where a child or qualifying young person normally lives with two or more persons who are not a couple, only one of them is to be treated as responsible and that is the person who has the main responsibility.
-- src:141 | (5) The persons mentioned in paragraph (4) may jointly nominate which of them has the main responsibility but the Secretary of State may determine that question—
-- src:142 | (a) in default of agreement; or
-- src:143 | (b) if a nomination or change of nomination does not, in the opinion of the Secretary of State, reflect the arrangements between those persons.
-- src:144 | (6) Subject to regulation 4A, a child or qualifying young person is to be treated as not being the responsibility of any person during any period when the child or qualifying young person is—
-- src:145 | (a) looked after by a local authority; or
-- src:146 | (b) a prisoner,
-- src:148 | (7) Where a child or qualifying young person is temporarily absent from a person's household the person ceases to be responsible for the child or qualifying young person if—
-- src:149 | (a) the absence is expected to exceed, or does exceed, 6 months; or
-- src:150 | (b) the absence is from Great Britain and is expected to exceed, or does exceed, one month unless it is in circumstances where an absence of a person for longer than one month would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2) or (3) (medical treatment or convalescence or death of close relative etc.).
@ref reg 4(1) to (7) (src:137-150)
GIVEN `responsible apart from paragraphs (6) and (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `treated as not the responsibility of any person under paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person ceases to be responsible under paragraph (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4 — the person is responsible for the child or qualifying young person` `responsible apart from paragraphs (6) and (7)` `treated as not the responsibility of any person under paragraph (6)` `the person ceases to be responsible under paragraph (7)` MEANS
    (`responsible apart from paragraphs (6) and (7)`)
    AND (NOT `treated as not the responsibility of any person under paragraph (6)`)
    AND (NOT `the person ceases to be responsible under paragraph (7)`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 4A: children looked after by a local authority.

-- (2) A person has parental responsibility if they are not a foster parent and, in England and Wales, they have parental
-- responsibility within the meaning of section 3 of the Children Act 1989 or, in Scotland, they have any or all of the legal
-- responsibilities or rights described in sections 1 or 2 of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995.
-- src:156 | (2) For the purposes of this regulation, a person has parental responsibility if they are not a foster parent and—
-- src:157 | (a) in England and Wales, they have parental responsibility within the meaning of section 3 of the Children Act 1989 ; or
-- src:158 | (b) in Scotland, they have any or all of the legal responsibilities or rights described in sections 1 or 2 of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995 .
@ref reg 4A(2) (src:156-158)
GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      `the person is a foster parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has parental responsibility within the meaning of section 3 of the Children Act 1989` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts on children (not a piece)
      `the person has any or all of the legal responsibilities or rights described in sections 1 or 2 of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts on children (not a piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4A(2) — the person has parental responsibility` nation `the person is a foster parent` `the person has parental responsibility within the meaning of section 3 of the Children Act 1989` `the person has any or all of the legal responsibilities or rights described in sections 1 or 2 of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995` MEANS
    (NOT `the person is a foster parent`)
    AND (CONSIDER nation
         WHEN England THEN `the person has parental responsibility within the meaning of section 3 of the Children Act 1989`
         WHEN Wales THEN `the person has parental responsibility within the meaning of section 3 of the Children Act 1989`
         WHEN Scotland THEN `the person has any or all of the legal responsibilities or rights described in sections 1 or 2 of the Children (Scotland) Act 1995`)

-- (1) Excluded from regulation 4(6)(a): (a) a planned short term break, or one of a series, for respite for the person who normally
-- cares; (b) any period during which the child or young person is placed with, or continues to live with, their parent or a person
-- with parental responsibility; (c) any period during which they are placed for adoption.
-- src:152 | (1) There is excluded from regulation 4(6)(a)—
-- src:153 | (a) any period which is in the nature of a planned short term break, or is one of a series of such breaks, for the purpose of providing respite for the person who normally cares for the child or qualifying young person;
-- src:154 | (b) any period during which the child or qualifying young person is placed with, or continues to live with, their parent or a person who has parental responsibility for them;
-- src:155 | (c) any period during which the child or qualifying young person is placed for adoption under the Adoption and Children Act 2002 or the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007.
@ref reg 4A(1) (src:152-155)
GIVEN `the period is in the nature of a planned short term break, or is one of a series of such breaks, for the purpose of providing respite for the person who normally cares for the child or qualifying young person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child or qualifying young person is placed with, or continues to live with, their parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child or qualifying young person is placed with, or continues to live with, a person who has parental responsibility for them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the child or qualifying young person is placed for adoption under the Adoption and Children Act 2002 or the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007` IS A BOOLEAN  -- out of range: other Acts on children (not a piece)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 4A(1) — the period is excluded from regulation 4(6)(a)` `the period is in the nature of a planned short term break, or is one of a series of such breaks, for the purpose of providing respite for the person who normally cares for the child or qualifying young person` `the child or qualifying young person is placed with, or continues to live with, their parent` `the child or qualifying young person is placed with, or continues to live with, a person who has parental responsibility for them` `the child or qualifying young person is placed for adoption under the Adoption and Children Act 2002 or the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007` MEANS
    (`the period is in the nature of a planned short term break, or is one of a series of such breaks, for the purpose of providing respite for the person who normally cares for the child or qualifying young person`)
    OR (`the child or qualifying young person is placed with, or continues to live with, their parent`)
    OR (`the child or qualifying young person is placed with, or continues to live with, a person who has parental responsibility for them`)
    OR (`the child or qualifying young person is placed for adoption under the Adoption and Children Act 2002 or the Adoption and Children (Scotland) Act 2007`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Regulation 5: qualifying young person.

-- (1) A person who has reached 16 but not 20 is a qualifying young person (a) up to, but not including, the 1st September following
-- their 16th birthday; and (b) up to, but not including, the 1st September following their 19th birthday, if enrolled on, or accepted
-- for, approved training or a course of education (i) which is not a course of advanced education, (ii) provided at a school or
-- college or elsewhere but approved by the Secretary of State, and (iii) where the average time spent during term time receiving
-- tuition, engaging in practical work or supervised study or taking examinations exceeds 12 hours per week.
-- (2) A person aged 19 must have started the education or training, or been enrolled on or accepted for it, before reaching 19.
-- (3) Education or training provided by a contract of employment is not included. (5) A person receiving universal credit, an
-- employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance is not a qualifying young person.
-- src:160 | (1) A person who has reached the age of 16 but not the age of 20 is a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 1 of the Act and these Regulations—
-- src:161 | (a) up to, but not including, the 1st September following their 16th birthday; and
-- src:162 | (b) up to, but not including, the 1st September following their 19th birthday, if they are enrolled on, or accepted for, approved training or a course of education—
-- src:163 | (i) which is not a course of advanced education,
-- src:164 | (ii) which is provided at a school or college or provided elsewhere but approved by the Secretary of State, and
-- src:165 | (iii) where the average time spent during term time in receiving tuition, engaging in practical work or supervised study or taking examinations exceeds 12 hours per week.
-- src:166 | (2) Where the young person is aged 19, they must have started the education or training or been enrolled on or accepted for it before reaching that age.
-- src:167 | (3) The education or training referred to in paragraph (1) does not include education or training provided by means of a contract of employment.
-- src:168 | (4) “Approved training” means training in pursuance of arrangements made under section 2(1) of the Employment and Training Act 1973 or section 2(3) of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990 which is approved by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this regulation.
-- src:169 | (5) A person who is receiving universal credit, an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance is not a qualifying young person.
@ref reg 5 (src:160-169)
DECLARE `Young person and the education or training` HAS
    `date of birth`                                                                                     IS A DATE
    `the person is enrolled on, or accepted for, approved training or a course of education`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the course is a course of advanced education`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the course is provided at a school or college, or elsewhere but approved by the Secretary of State`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the average time spent during term time in tuition, practical work, supervised study or examinations`  IS A NUMBER  -- hours per week
    `the person started the education or training, or was enrolled on or accepted for it, before reaching the age of 19`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the education or training is provided by means of a contract of employment`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is receiving universal credit`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person is receiving`                                                                            IS A LIST OF Benefit

-- (1)(b)(i) to (iii) and (2) and (3): the education or training that extends the status to the 1st September after the 19th birthday.
-- src:162 | (b) up to, but not including, the 1st September following their 19th birthday, if they are enrolled on, or accepted for, approved training or a course of education—
-- src:163 | (i) which is not a course of advanced education,
-- src:164 | (ii) which is provided at a school or college or provided elsewhere but approved by the Secretary of State, and
-- src:165 | (iii) where the average time spent during term time in receiving tuition, engaging in practical work or supervised study or taking examinations exceeds 12 hours per week.
-- src:166 | (2) Where the young person is aged 19, they must have started the education or training or been enrolled on or accepted for it before reaching that age.
-- src:167 | (3) The education or training referred to in paragraph (1) does not include education or training provided by means of a contract of employment.
@ref reg 5(1)(b), (2) and (3) (src:162-167)
GIVEN person IS A `Young person and the education or training`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 5(1)(b) — the education or training extends the status to the 1st September following the 19th birthday` person day MEANS
    (person's `the person is enrolled on, or accepted for, approved training or a course of education`)
    AND (NOT (person's `the course is a course of advanced education`))
    AND (person's `the course is provided at a school or college, or elsewhere but approved by the Secretary of State`)
    AND ((person's `the average time spent during term time in tuition, practical work, supervised study or examinations`) GREATER THAN 12)
    AND (NOT (person's `the education or training is provided by means of a contract of employment`))
    AND ((`uc1 — the age in complete years on a date` (person's `date of birth`) day LESS THAN 19)
         OR (person's `the person started the education or training, or was enrolled on or accepted for it, before reaching the age of 19`))

-- src:160 | (1) A person who has reached the age of 16 but not the age of 20 is a qualifying young person for the purposes of Part 1 of the Act and these Regulations—
-- src:161 | (a) up to, but not including, the 1st September following their 16th birthday; and
-- src:162 | (b) up to, but not including, the 1st September following their 19th birthday, if they are enrolled on, or accepted for, approved training or a course of education—
-- src:163 | (i) which is not a course of advanced education,
-- src:164 | (ii) which is provided at a school or college or provided elsewhere but approved by the Secretary of State, and
-- src:165 | (iii) where the average time spent during term time in receiving tuition, engaging in practical work or supervised study or taking examinations exceeds 12 hours per week.
-- src:166 | (2) Where the young person is aged 19, they must have started the education or training or been enrolled on or accepted for it before reaching that age.
-- src:167 | (3) The education or training referred to in paragraph (1) does not include education or training provided by means of a contract of employment.
-- src:168 | (4) “Approved training” means training in pursuance of arrangements made under section 2(1) of the Employment and Training Act 1973 or section 2(3) of the Enterprise and New Towns (Scotland) Act 1990 which is approved by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this regulation.
-- src:169 | (5) A person who is receiving universal credit, an employment and support allowance or a jobseeker's allowance is not a qualifying young person.
@ref reg 5 (src:160-169)
GIVEN person IS A `Young person and the education or training`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 5 — the person is a qualifying young person on a day` person day MEANS
    `has reached 16 but not 20`
    AND (`before the 1st September following the 16th birthday`
         OR (`reg 5(1)(b) — the education or training extends the status to the 1st September following the 19th birthday` person day
             AND `before the 1st September following the 19th birthday`))
    AND (NOT (person's `the person is receiving universal credit`))
    AND (NOT ((elem `employment and support allowance` (person's `the person is receiving`))
              OR (elem `jobseeker's allowance` (person's `the person is receiving`))))
    WHERE
        `has reached 16 but not 20` MEANS
            (`uc1 — the age in complete years on a date` (person's `date of birth`) day AT LEAST 16)
            AND (`uc1 — the age in complete years on a date` (person's `date of birth`) day LESS THAN 20)
        `before the 1st September following the 16th birthday` MEANS
            day LESS THAN (`uc1 — the 1st September following a birthday` (person's `date of birth`) 16)
        `before the 1st September following the 19th birthday` MEANS
            day LESS THAN (`uc1 — the 1st September following a birthday` (person's `date of birth`) 19)

